  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 0.2.6\n\n- Update Microsoft.Extensions dependencies to 10.0.13 while retaining support for .NET 8, 9 and 10.\n\n## 0.2.5\n\n- Render Contract rules, including scenarios and path captures, through Gapfy.Echo.Contracts.\n- Return the hosted 502 problem response for missing or invalid contracts without calling the real service.\n- Apply the hosted Contract header and active-content policy; preserve Static behavior and existing delay limits.\n\n## Service change on 2026-09-14\n\n- Echo moved the rule feed to the paid plans. This was a service change, not a package release: an already installed 0.2.3 client can stop obtaining rules on Free without this package changing.\n- With no rules loaded, opted-in calls continue to the real service and the failed refresh is logged. Rules already in memory or on disk remain active until the package is disarmed or its cache is cleared.\n\n## 0.2.3\n\n- Align the package version with the readable contract JSON release; mock client behavior is unchanged.\n\n## 0.2.2\n\n- Expose hosted authoring validation for response headers, content types, UTF-8 body size and route patterns.\n- Validate patterns with the same matcher used at runtime and preserve desktop source parity.\n- Apply the public host allowlist for authoring; the embedded server package retains its configurable header policy.\n- Correct public documentation and product links.\n- Include NuGet release notes and symbols in the coordinated Echo package release.\n\n## 0.2.0\n\n- Read the hierarchical rule feed shared with the mock server package.\n- Preserve the explicit opt-in for each HTTP client and the existing production and failure guards.\n\n## 0.1.1\n\n- Resolve rooted request paths consistently on every OS instead of parsing them as file URIs on Linux.\n\n## 0.1.0\n\n- Introduce opt-in interception for `IHttpClientFactory` clients using Echo mock rules.\n- Fail open and refresh rule snapshots without blocking application startup.\n- Refuse to arm in Production.",
